.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt SMP-SERVER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm smp-server
.Nd SimpleX Messaging Protocol server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm init
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Ar host
.Nm
.Cm start
.Op Fl l
.Nm
.Cm delete
.Nm
.Cm help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a message broker that implements the SimpleX Messaging Protocol
(SMP). It provides end-to-end encrypted message relay without
storing user identifiers or unencrypted message content.
.Pp
The server must be initialized once before first use.
The
.Cm init
command creates configuration files, TLS credentials, and
persistent storage under
.Pa /etc/simplex/smp-server/
and
.Pa /var/simplex/smp-server/ .
.Pp
The
.Cm start
command runs the server in the foreground.
The
.Cm delete
command removes the server configuration and all stored data.
.Pp
The
.Fl l
flag enables logging to stdout in addition
to the log file.
The
.Fl p Ar port
option overrides the default port 5223.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/simplex/smp-server/
Configuration files and TLS credentials.
.It Pa /var/simplex/smp-server/
Persistent message store, queues, and logs.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr simplex-chat 1 ,
.Xr xftp-server 1
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T SimpleX Messaging Protocol
.%U https://github.com/simplex-chat/simplexmq/blob/stable/protocol/simplex-messaging.md
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An SimpleX Chat contributors
